  "historical_output_text": " \n\nPhotosyethsis\nDefinition\nThe term refers primarily, although in some cases only implicitly and metaphorically or figurativley, in biological and physical chemistry to any process that produces organic material using carbon as energy from the inactivation by radiation (sun light) to water.\n\nCentral ideas:\nOrganism obtains nutrients for energy.\nRadiated sunlight acts an activiation mechanism, initiating the conversion\nWater molecules split, liberate the electron for use.\n\nSeuqnce:\n\nPlastoids in Chloroplasas of the plants capture photons of radiation from Sun.  The radiation energy splits Water molecule (2H_0) in to  8 Hydrogen atom + Oxygen molecule 4 H +1  2H0 + O2 \nThese hydrogen molecules combine, along with other materials to synthesize organic matter, primarily Glucoz.\n",
